@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+---
+id: dl-001-use-half-open-utc-day-intervals-for-rentals
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use half-open UTC day intervals for rentals"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Rentals must cover complete UTC calendar days, and adjacent rentals of the same item must be possible.
+
+## Decision
+
+Represent a rental period as the half-open interval `[start, end)`. Both boundaries must be valid
+UTC ISO-8601 timestamps at midnight, and `end` must be after `start`. Calculate the total as the
+number of 24-hour days in the interval multiplied by the integer-cent daily price. Overlap exists
+when each interval starts before the other ends.
+
+Booking identifiers will be deterministic, sequential values generated by the service instance.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The end boundary is the start of the day after the final rented day, so a booking ending at midnight
+does not conflict with one starting at that same midnight. This also avoids randomness and wall-clock
+dependencies. Cancellation and refund calculation remain out of scope until cancellation is added.
